BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:presidents-day-20270215@todaycelebrates.com
DTSTAMP:20261014T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270215
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270216
SUMMARY:Presidents' Day
DESCRIPTION:The federal holiday on the third Monday in February is\, in law
 \, Washington's Birthday. Congress has never renamed it: "Presidents' Day"
  was proposed in 1951\, got nowhere officially\, and became the common nam
 e three decades later through holiday sales advertising. The holiday also 
 cannot land on Washington's birthday — the third Monday in February fall
 s between the 15th and the 21st\, and he was born on the 22nd.\n\nhttps://
 todaycelebrates.com/holiday/presidents-day/
URL;VALUE=URI:https://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/presidents-day/
CATEGORIES:Community
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CLASS:PUBLIC
SEQUENCE:0
END:VEVENT
